              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ડાબું (ḍābũ) is listed by CDIAL, glossed \"left\", under ḍavva, \"left-hand, crosswise\", and its variant ḍābba, reconstructed forms. CDIAL calls the group non-Aryan and cites A. Master, who traced it to Dravidian (CDIAL 5539); DEDR sets it beside Dravidian words for left, such as Telugu ḍā (DEDR 449)."
